  "result": "Perfect! All 99 tests pass. I've successfully added comprehensive VAT support to the invoicing system:\n\n\u2705 **New helper functions in src/invoices.js**\n- `lineDiscount(line)` - calculates discount amount\n- `lineVAT(line)` - calculates VAT on amount after discount, rounded per line\n\n\u2705 **Updated invoiceTotals** returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n- VAT calculated per line: (amount after discount) \u00d7 (vatRate / 100)\n- Each line VAT rounded individually using roundCents()\n- Invoice VAT = sum of all rounded line VATs\n- `total = subtotal - discount + vat` (clamped at 0)\n\n\u2705 **Updated renderInvoiceText**\n- Shows VAT line just above total (only if VAT > 0)\n- Displays: `VAT: \u20acamount`\n- All amounts formatted with formatEuros()\n\n\u2705 **12 new tests** covering:\n- lineDiscount and lineVAT calculations\n- VAT with different rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n- VAT after discount (correctly rounded)\n- Multiple lines with mixed VAT rates\n- Render output with VAT breakdown\n- Edge cases (exempt items, 0% VAT lines)\n\nThe decision is implemented: VAT is always calculated per line on the amount after discount, rounded per line, and the invoice VAT is the sum of those rounded amounts\u2014never a percentage of the invoice total.",
